  "Notes": "Lineage 2 Prominence - 0.1.9\n\nWeapons and crafting\n- Updated weapon progression, combat values, level requirements and tooltips.\n- Weapon shops now offer level-1 weapons through a single Buy Weapons menu.\n- Expanded T1 and T2 crafting coverage, with recipes in Humble Beginnings and Gaining Momentum exchanges and keys in the matching village shops.\n- T2 recipes use three keys worth 10% each, with the remaining material cost distributed by equipment type. Recipe scrolls are worth 10% of the finished item.\n- Rebuilt dual swords and dual daggers into 61 progressive pairings each. Obtain them by combining two weapons at a blacksmith; the base fee is the dual weapon value minus both component values. Names, appearances and splitting match the new pairs.\n- Removed obsolete dual weapons. Existing copies are removed during maintenance and their owners receive the weapons' base adena value automatically. No claim or token exchange is needed.\n\nMovement and skills\n- Improved momentum recovery after brief movement-key releases and corrected autorun chase turning and camera control.\n- Fixed stuck movement and mouse inputs after switching away from the game.\n- Heal and Chant of Life unlock at level 10; Meditate unlocks at level 12 for starting Mystics.\n\nLauncher\n- Launcher updates now take priority over client updates. Play remains unavailable until both are current.\n\nTo apply: close Lineage II, click Update launcher if offered, then Update.\n",
